## Q15 (gui-stack-v1-issues) — a class nested in a `module` must resolve its
## own fields inside method bodies. Before the fix `self.value` failed with
## "no field value on type Signal" because `self` was typed with the bare
## class name while the class def was registered under its qualified name
## (`Quiver.Signal`). Covers a generic module class constructed + a method
## reading a field, plus a non-generic one.

module Quiver
  class Signal[T]
    value: T
    def init(@value: T)
    end
    def get -> T
      self.value
    end
  end

  class Counter
    n: Int
    def init(@n: Int)
    end
    def bump -> Int
      self.n + 1
    end
  end
end

def main
  let s = Quiver.Signal.new(42)
  puts "v=#{s.get}"
  let c = Quiver.Counter.new(10)
  puts "c=#{c.bump}"
end
